      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Derelict Cottage, Outbuildings & Approx. 51.27 Acres in West Clare\n\nA rare opportunity to acquire a traditional stone-built cottage, substantial outbuildings and approximately 51.27 acres (20.75 hectares) of land in an elevated countryside setting in West Clare.\n\nDating back to circa 1890, this character-filled cottage offers enormous potential for those looking to create a unique country home, establish a rural retreat or acquire a substantial landholding with existing buildings.\n\nThe cottage extends to approximately 700 sq. ft. and is in need of complete renovation, providing the successful purchaser with a blank canvas to restore and reimagine the property to suit their own requirements.\n\nSubject to qualifying criteria, the property may have potential to benefit from the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant and applicable SEAI energy upgrade grants. Prospective purchasers should satisfy themselves independently as to eligibility and the availability of any grants.\n\nThe Cottage\nThe traditional stone-built cottage has a slate roof and currently comprises a parlour and three additional rooms, together with a lean-to shed.\n\nThe property requires full renovation and modernisation, including plumbing, electrics, insulation, windows and associated works.\n\nElectricity is connected to the cottage, with water available from a private scheme and well.\n\nOutbuildings\nA major feature of the property is the selection of traditional outbuildings, adding further character and potential to the holding.\n\nOutbuilding 1 extends to approximately 600 sq. ft. and incorporates a cow house and storage cabins beneath a corrugated iron roof.\n\nOutbuilding 2 is also stone-built with a corrugated iron roof and has previously been used for housing animals. An attached cattle crush is also in place.\n\nApprox. 51.27 Acres\nThe lands extend to approximately 51.27 acres / 20.75 hectares and comprise a mix of spring/summer grazing ground and forestry.\n\nApproximately 20 acres are under forestry, planted in 2007, providing an interesting mix of agricultural and forestry land within the overall holding.\n\nThe combination of extensive acreage, traditional buildings and an elevated setting makes this an attractive proposition for a variety of potential purchasers.\n\nLocation\nCloonlaheen Middle enjoys a peaceful rural location while remaining within convenient reach of the amenities and coastline of West Clare.\n\nThe property is approximately:\n\n• 9.3km from Connolly Village\n• 11km from Miltown Malbay\n• 11km from Spanish Point\n• 25km from Ennis\n\nThe location offers an appealing balance of countryside living with convenient access to nearby towns, villages and the renowned West Clare coastline.\n\nProperty at a Glance\nAMV: 225,000\nLand: Approx. 51.27 acres / 20.75 hectares\nForestry: Approx. 20 acres\nCottage: Approx. 700 sq. ft.\nBedrooms: 2\nOutbuildings: Two traditional stone-built outbuildings\nBER: Exempt\nWater: Private scheme & well\nElectricity: Connected\nFolio: CE9289\nCoordinates: 52.806798, -9.306693\n\nFor purchasers searching for a renovation project with significant acreage in West Clare, Cloonlaheen Middle presents an opportunity that is becoming increasingly difficult to find.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the setting, extent of the lands and potential this property has to offer."
      },
